{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-325351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(5,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{4}{3})(x-5) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,\\frac{4}{3}(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-325351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}(x-5)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(0,-2),\\,a=\\sqrt{16}=4,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny+2=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-10472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}x"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{4}{9}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}(x-2)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}(x-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+2=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-165470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-165470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(2,-2),\\,a=\\sqrt{16}=4,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny+2=\\pm \\frac{2}{4}(x-2)\\,\\,y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}(x-2).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-165470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-165470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-165470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+2=\\pm 2(x-2)"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}(x-2)"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}(x-4)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x+2)"] ["math" "y-4=\\pm 2(x+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-165470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}(x-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(0,-2),\\,a=\\sqrt{25}=5,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny+2=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-86650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}(x+2)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}(x-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+2=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $(x-7)^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ((h,k)) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(7,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{1}=1,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{3}{1})(x-7) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,3(x-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-325348" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325348" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3(x-7)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-84071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-84071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4,\\,h=0,\\,k=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny-1=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-84071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-84071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-84071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}x"] ["math" "y-3=\\pm (x-4)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}(x-1)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}(x-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-84071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y-1=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{4}=2,\\,b=\\sqrt{36}=6,\\,h=0,\\,k=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-6) & =\\pm (\\frac{2}{6})(x-0) \\\\ y+6 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4