).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-10470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{3}{5}(x+2)"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}(x+2)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{3}{5}(x-2)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}(x-2)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{9}{5}(x-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10470" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y-2=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}(x-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{3},\\,b=\\sqrt{2},\\,h=-1,\\,k=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-1) & =\\pm (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}})(x-(-1)) \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-16436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+1=\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}(x+1)"] ["math" "y+1=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}(x+1)"] ["math" "y+1=\\pm \\sqrt{2}(x+1)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}(x-1)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\sqrt{3}(x-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+1=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}(x+1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{27}-\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{12}=1.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(4,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3},\\,b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}})(x-4) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,\\frac{3}{2}(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-325367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}(x-4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-83906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $16{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-64x-2y+47=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-83906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-64x-2y+47 & =0 \\\\ (16{x}^{2}-64x)+(-{y}^{2}-2y)+47 & =0 \\\\ 16[{x}^{2}-4x]-[{y}^{2}+2y]+47 & =0 \\\\ 16[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y+1)^{2}-1]+47 & =0 \\\\ 16(x-2)^{2}-64-(y+1)^{2}+1+47 & =0 \\\\ 16(x-2)^{2}-(y+1)^{2} & =64-1-47 \\\\ 16(x-2)^{2}-(y+1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{16(x-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{16}{16} \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nh=2,\\,k=-1,\\,a=\\sqrt{1}=1,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{1}(x-2) \\\\  & =\\pm 4(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-83906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-83906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-83906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+1=\\pm 4(x-2)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x+2)"] ["math" "y-2=(x-2)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x+1)"] ["math" "y-4=\\pm 2(x+1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-83906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+1=\\pm 4(x-2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}+16x-20=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ terms and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}+16x-20 & =0 \\\\ (4{x}^{2}+16x)-9{y}^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}+4x]-9{y}^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x+2)^{2}-4]-9{y}^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-16-9{y}^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =20+16 \\\\ 4(x+2)^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{4(x+2)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{36} & =\\frac{36}{36} \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nh=-2,\\,k=0,\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-86672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x+2)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}(x+2)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}(x-2)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}(x+2)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{3}(x+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-86672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x+2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-24x=0.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Group the $x$ terms and complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-24x & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-6x)-9{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4\\,[(x-3)^{2}-9]-9{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4(x-3)^{2}-36-9{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4(x-3)^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{4(x-3)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus it is a horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nso the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nHere,\n\n$$\n(h,k)=(3,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{2}{3})(x-3) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,\\frac{2}{3}(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-325375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}(x-3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+8x+7=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+8x+7 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x-{y}^{2}+7 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16-{y}^{2}+7 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-{y}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(-4,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny=\\pm (x+4).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-16443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+4=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}x"] ["math" "y+4=\\pm x"] ["math" "y=\\pm (x+4)"] ["math" "y=\\pm 3(x+4)"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}(x+4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-16443" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm (x+4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-32x+18y+19=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-32x+18y+19 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x-9{y}^{2}+18y+19 & =0 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-8x]-9[{y}^{2}-2y]+19 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-4)^{2}-16]-9[(y-1)^{2}-1]+19 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)^{2}-64-9(y-1)^{2}+9+19 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)^{2}-9(y-1)^{2} & =64-9-19 \\\\ 4(x-4)^{2}-9(y-1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(4,1),\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny-1=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x-4).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-10476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+1=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x+4)"] ["math" "y+1=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}(x+4)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x-4)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}(x-4)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}(x-4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-10476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y-1=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}(x-4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}+36y-16{x}^{2}+32x-124=0.$\n\n$y\\,\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$=\\pm $\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}+36y-16{x}^{2}+32x-124 & =0 \\\\ 9({y}^{2}+4y)-16({x}^{2}-2x)-124 & =0 \\\\ 9\\,[(y+2)^{2}-4]-16\\,[(x-1)^{2}-1]-124 & =0 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-36-16(x-1)^{2}+16-124 & =0 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-16(x-1)^{2} & =144 \\\\ \\frac{9(y+2)^{2}}{144}-\\frac{16(x-1)^{2}}{144} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a vertical hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(1,-2),\\,a=\\sqrt{16}=4,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-2) & =\\pm (\\frac{4}{3})(x-1) \\\\ y+2 & =\\pm \\,\\frac{4}{3}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9d5154da0cfce74ec086f94646f720f625915de51a24fa5b3c3e0f11658bcaa4"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325439" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}(x-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+54y-27=0.$\n\n$y\\,\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$=\\pm $\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ terms and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+54y-27 & =0 \\\\ 9({y}^{2}+6y)-4{x}^{2}-27 & =0 \\\\ 9\\,[(y+3)^{2}-9]-4{x}^{2}-27 & =0 \\\\ 9(y+3)^{2}-81-4{x}^{2}-27 & =0 \\\\ 9(y+3)^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =108 \\\\ \\frac{9(y+3)^{2}}{108}-\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{108} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{27} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a vertical hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(0,-3),\\,a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3},\\,b=\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-3) & =\\pm (\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}})(x-0) \\\\ y+3 & =\\pm \\,\\frac{2}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060522/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9f652b753b77fc91fa788e0352f8f45171f84dce87b3831152801507b6c9d9e"} {"question" "q-325436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r